The white gull seeks the open sea;
The partridge loves the woodland dim :;
The robin in his ecstasy


Seeks for his song the elm tree $


limb;


The hawk patrols the sapphire sky;
The blackbird in the sedges hides;
The catbird hunts the bush nearbv


Where in the nest her Aedgling bides.
ne locust, all the summer day.


Sings loudest in the blazing sun;
he hawkmoth roams the twilight gray
And sips the roses, one by one;
ne clover yields the roaming bee
Its sweetness of the summer hour:
The butterfly pcrsistently


lnvades the heart of eyerv flower
The wind pursues the drifting cloud ::
The sunlight strikes the lake with


fire;


lhe waterfall, with clamor loud


Forever seeks it's hearts desire:
Inc wild deer range the upland lea
The swallow wings across the blue;
